From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] cuda: cap MMQ J tile near the expected MoE expert segment width

mul_mat_q_switch_J picks J from ncols_max, the worst-case column count of
a single expert segment (= n_tokens for mul_mat_id). With 256 experts and
top-8 routing the segments average ncols_dst/nchannels_y columns - 16 at
ub512, an 8x overshoot - so every expert's single J=128 tile is ~87%
masked padding that the WMMA loop still computes. Q4_K gate/up and Q5_K
down expert GEMMs are 43.6% of pp512 kernel time on this box.

Cap J for the ids path at the smallest valid config >= 2x the expected
segment width (2x headroom for routing imbalance; 16 floor). At ub512
this selects J=32: expert tiles are mostly single, near-full column
blocks. The grid still covers worst-case imbalance because ntx grows as J
shrinks and out-of-range tiles exit before any tile work. Weight traffic
is unchanged (a <=32-column expert still loads its slab once). Dense
matmuls (ids_dst == null) are untouched; decode expert matvecs route via
mmvq, not MMQ. GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MMQ_MOE_J restores stock selection.

Measured (runner box, pinned device 0). J sweep at pp512 (single process):
stock-J 3197, J=16 3650, J=32 3911, J=48 3810, J=64 3728 tok/s. Same-
binary toggle A/B, 5 interleaved rounds: pp512 3181-3225 off vs 3885-3933
on, median per-round ratio 1.2216; tg128 identical (112.2-112.9 both
arms). Whole-process stock-vs-cand A/B (full series): pp512 median ratio
1.2226, tg128 1.389. Ranked-style llama-server uncached 533-token prompt:
2065 -> 2525 tok/s prefill (+22.3% - holds at server level, kernel-time
lever). Gate ppl (-c 512 --chunks 8): cand 3.9177/3.9180 vs stock
3.9314x2 (-0.35%, band +/-0.5%; the cap itself moves the 0022 build only
+0.07%). Server greedy identity byte-exact off vs on, long and short
prompts.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
index 2eb15fdfa..360eff138 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
@@ -1493,6 +1493,35 @@ void mul_mat_q_switch_J(ggml_backend_cuda_context & ctx, const mmq_args & args,
         }
     }
 
+    // MoE (mul_mat_id): J is otherwise chosen from ncols_max, the worst-case
+    // column count of a single expert segment. With many experts the segments
+    // average ncols_dst/nchannels_y columns - far below ncols_max - so a
+    // ncols_max-sized J tile is mostly masked padding that the MMA loop still
+    // computes. Cap J near the expected segment width (2x headroom for routing
+    // imbalance); the grid covers the worst case regardless because ntx grows
+    // as J shrinks, and out-of-range tiles exit before any tile work.
+    if (args.ids_dst != nullptr && args.nchannels_y > 1 &&
+        getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MMQ_MOE_J") == nullptr) {
+        const int64_t cols_per_expert = (args.ncols_dst + args.nchannels_y - 1) / args.nchannels_y;
+        int64_t target = 2*cols_per_expert;
+        if (target < 16) {
+            target = 16;
+        }
+        if (target < J_best) {
+            for (int J = 8; J <= 128; J += 8) {
+                const ggml_cuda_mmq_config config = ggml_cuda_mmq_get_config(type, J, fallback, cc);
+                if (config.type == GGML_TYPE_COUNT || J < target) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                if (mmq_get_nbytes_shared(config, cc) > smpbo) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                J_best = J;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     switch (J_best) {
         case   8:
             launch_mul_mat_q<type,   8, fallback>(ctx, args, stream);
